# FORGE — Mobile Standards

## Architecture

- Feature folders: `data` / `presentation` / domain logic in repositories.
- API abstraction via `core/network`; no raw HTTP in widgets.
- Reuse `forge_card`, motion tokens, and shared patterns from `lib/core`.

## UX & Performance

- Offline-first mindset: cache watch history, graceful offline states.
- Background-friendly uploads; adaptive video quality on watch.
- Efficient lists; avoid rebuilding entire trees on minor state changes.

## Platform Readiness

- Deep links via router (`app_router.dart`); push notification hooks when adding features.
- Secure token storage; session refresh aligned with API JWT/refresh flow.

## Consistency with Web

- Same creator-first, skill-learning identity — not a generic video app shell.
- Parity on critical flows: auth, watch, studio upload, notifications, live.

## Testing & Changes

- Match Dart conventions in repo; minimal scope per PR.
- Validate on both iOS and Android paths when touching platform channels.
